On this week's episode of <a href="https://podcasts.apple.com/us/podcast/whats-next-for-iphone-duo/id1602394741?i=1000803134129">The MacRumors Show</a>, we discuss the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-duo/">iPhone Duo</a>'s new Face Unlock feature and all of the latest rumors about Apple's next-generation foldable iPhone.<br/>
<br/>
<div class="center-wrap"><iframe width="560" height="315" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/LR64rANGkFo?si=Bfv2UtnuLv4bBWMf" title="YouTube video player" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen></iframe><em>Subscribe to <a href="https://www.youtube.com/@themacrumorsshow?sub_confirmation=1">The MacRumors Show</a> YouTube channel for more videos</em></div><br/>
Apple this week added "<a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/16/iphone-duo-face-unlock-hands-on/">Unlock with Front Camera</a>" to the existing &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj; in iOS 27.3 beta 2. The optional feature allows users to unlock the phone with facial recognition when it is closed, providing an alternative to the side-mounted <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/touch-id/">Touch ID</a> sensor. It does not offer <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/mask-face-id/">Face ID</a>'s depth-sensing authentication, and &zwnj;Touch ID&zwnj; remains necessary for <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/apple-pay/">Apple Pay</a> and accessing saved passwords.<br/>
<br/>
The addition makes unlocking more convenient when fingerprint recognition is impractical, such as with wet hands, but introduces a distinction between unlocking the phone and authenticating sensitive actions. The same beta adds "<a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/16/ios-27-3-beta-2-everything-new/">Close to Lock</a>," allowing users to lock the device when folding it shut instead of transferring their app to the outer display.<br/>
<br/>
<ul><br/>
<li><a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/16/iphone-duo-face-unlock-hands-on/">Hands-On With the iPhone Duo's New Face Unlock</a></li></ul><br/>
<br/>
&zwnj;Face ID&zwnj; remains one of the biggest questions surrounding the next &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj;. <em>Bloomberg</em>'s <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/22/iphone-duo-2-prototypes-under-display-face-id/">Mark Gurman</a> says Apple has developed second-generation prototypes with &zwnj;Face ID&zwnj; beneath the outer display, but subsequently warned that the company is <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/15/apple-aims-to-upgrade-iphone-duo-in-four-ways/">running out of time</a> to finalize the feature. It could instead arrive with the third generation.<br/>
<br/>
Meanwhile, the leaker known as "Digital Chat Station" claims current engineering units <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/18/iphone-duo-2-likely-to-retain-touch-id/">retain Touch ID</a>, a 7.6-inch inner display, and a 5.4-inch outer display. &zwnj;Face ID&zwnj; limited to the outside would also leave a practical question about authentication when the phone is unfolded, potentially giving Apple a reason to retain fingerprint recognition alongside facial authentication.<br/>
<br/>
The second-generation &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj; is expected to launch in the fall of 2027. Its development reportedly received <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/06/25/iphone-ultra-2-development-approved-by-apple/">formal approval</a> earlier this year, and Apple was already said to be <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/06/17/apple-testing-four-new-products-ios-28/">testing it</a> with iOS 28 in June.<br/>
<br/>
Apple's longer-term goals reportedly include a thinner and lighter design, a dedicated telephoto camera, and Action button functionality. Gurman previously <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/14/third-gen-iphone-duo-face-id-telephoto-lens/">predicted</a> that smaller components and computational processing could enable &zwnj;Face ID&zwnj; and a telephoto camera by the third generation.<br/>
<br/>
Gurman says a <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/08/09/iphone-ultra-3-rumored-to-feature-larger-displays/">third-generation model</a> could arrive as early as 2028 with slightly larger inner and outer displays. He separately discussed a potential inner screen of around 7.9 to 8.1 inches for a future model, rather than a separate larger "Max" version. A bigger chassis could provide more room for additional hardware, but would also raise questions about added weight.<br/>
<br/>
The leaker known as "Fixed Focus Digital" has <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/28/macbook-pro-hinge-iphone-duo-2/">linked improvements</a> in the touchscreen <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/macbook-pro/">MacBook Pro</a>'s hinge to work on the second- and third-generation &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj;. Reliability remains part of the discussion following <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/26/iphone-duo-crack-apple-response/">reports of cracked displays</a> on the current model. <br/>
<br/>
For the controls, Apple could restore the missing Action button's functionality without adding another physical button. According to the leaker known as "Instant Digital," iPhones launching from the second half of 2027 could <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/06/apple-rumored-to-drop-the-action-button/">combine the controls</a>, using a single press to open the camera and a long press for a customizable action.<br/>
